counterfactuals.output:
A method for producing a rapidly solidified metal strip, comprising:

supplying a molten metal to an outer peripheral surface of a cooling roll through an injection nozzle;

blocking an airflow flowing along the outer peripheral surface of the cooling roll at a position upstream, in a rotational direction of the cooling roll, of the injection nozzle;

introducing carbon dioxide gas onto the outer peripheral surface of the cooling roll at or near a molten-metal supply region; and

removing foreign matter from the outer peripheral surface of the cooling roll before the airflow is blocked.

In one embodiment, the foreign matter is removed by a cleaning device disposed upstream of an airflow-blocking member with respect to the rotational direction of the cooling roll. The airflow-blocking member suppresses entrainment of ambient air into a gap between the injection nozzle and the cooling roll. The carbon dioxide gas is supplied to the roll surface so as to form a gas atmosphere between the injection nozzle and the cooling roll, thereby improving stability of molten-metal contact with the cooling roll and reducing surface defects in the resulting solidified strip.

A corresponding apparatus may comprise:

a rotatable cooling roll configured to receive molten metal from an injection nozzle;

an airflow-blocking member disposed upstream of the injection nozzle in a rotational direction of the cooling roll and configured to restrict airflow along the roll surface;

a carbon dioxide gas supply unit configured to introduce carbon dioxide gas onto the surface of the cooling roll; and

a foreign-matter removing unit disposed upstream of the airflow-blocking member and configured to remove deposits, particles, oxides, or other foreign matter from the roll surface before the roll surface reaches the airflow-blocking member.
